Falsifies `designware_mobile_storage::proofs::a_chain_describes_its_bytes_inside_the_region`.

The defect: the last descriptor holds a whole page whatever is left, so a transfer that is not a
whole number of pages describes more bytes than the command moves, and the IDMAC waits on a
descriptor the card will never fill.

Expected to fail: `assert!(i * PAGE_BYTES + size == bytes)`, on any `bytes` that is not a multiple of a page.

diff --git a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/internal_direct_memory_access.rs b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/internal_direct_memory_access.rs
--- a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/internal_direct_memory_access.rs
+++ b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/internal_direct_memory_access.rs
@@ -296,11 +296,7 @@
     } else {
         word_0 |= DESCRIPTOR_DISABLE_INTERRUPT_ON_COMPLETION;
     }
-    let size = if last {
-        bytes - i * PAGE_BYTES
-    } else {
-        PAGE_BYTES
-    };
+    let size = PAGE_BYTES;
     let next = if last { 0 } else { i + 1 };
     [
         word_0,
